      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=ปัญหา: {{ $('Start').first().json.clean_text.match(/ปัญหา\\s*\\s*([\\s\\S]*)/)?.[1].trim() }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=Role: IT Support Classifier.\nCategory Context: {{ $('Core Agent').item.json.output.category }}\nBranch Name: {{ $('FInd Branch').item.json.output.branch_name }}\n\nTASK: Classify the user issue into the best Sub-Category from the provided list.\n\nSUB-CATEGORY LIST:\n{{ \n(() => {\n  const inputCat = $('Core Agent').item.json.output.category;\n  const mapCat = { \n    'SW': 'Software', \n    'HW': 'Hardware', \n    'CAMERA': 'Camera', \n    'NETWORK': 'Network', \n    'POS': 'Software',\n    'RATE': 'Software' \n  }[inputCat] || inputCat; \n\n  return $('Get Sub Category').all()\n    .filter(item => item.json.sub_category === mapCat || item.json.sub_category === inputCat)\n    .map(item => {\n        const aliasInfo = item.json.alias ? ` [Keywords: ${item.json.alias}]` : '';\n        return `- ${item.json.name}${aliasInfo}`;\n    })\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n})() \n}}\n\nRULES:\n1. ROOT CAUSE OVERRIDES SYMPTOM: When \"การแก้ไขปัญหา\" (Resolution) is present in the input, you MUST logically extract the actual root cause of the problem. Users typically report surface-level symptoms (e.g., UI display issues, software freezing, unable to print), but the resolution explicitly states the underlying failing component (e.g., server, infrastructure, network equipment, hardware). Your classification MUST strictly map to the underlying component that was fixed or identified in the resolution, completely overriding the initial symptom.\n2. PRINTER PRIORITY: If query mentions \"Printer/Paper\", select \"Printer\" immediately.\n3. BRANCH MAPPING: For NETWORK category, prioritize \"Internet PPontime\" only if the \"Branch Name\" has a 100% exact match in its keywords. If multiple ISPs contain the same branch name, cross-check with the issue intensity or use a pre-defined mapping table.\n4. IMPACT: Prioritize work-blocking issues (Login/Transaction) over cosmetic ones.\n5. FALLBACK RULE: If the issue does not fit any sub-category from the provided list, or if the list is empty, you must return the value of the \"Category Context\" as the sub_category.\n\nReturn ONLY the Sub-Category name."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
